1
00:00:00,600 --> 00:00:01,133
<i> Is that Godfather?</i>

2
00:00:01,267 --> 00:00:02,100
<i> Yes, that's him.</i>

3
00:00:02,233 --> 00:00:03,500
<i> Wow, Ma'am Yvette.</i>

4
00:00:03,633 --> 00:00:05,600
<i>This party is absolutely
stunning!</i>

5
00:00:05,733 --> 00:00:09,133
<i>Jin Ho, who is this
Catalina Esperanza?</i>

6
00:00:09,267 --> 00:00:11,300
<i>She just gave it to you,
just like that?</i>

7
00:00:11,433 --> 00:00:12,800
<i> I just got what we needed.</i>

8
00:00:12,933 --> 00:00:15,533
<i>Jin Ho is finding a way
to get inside.</i>

9
00:00:15,667 --> 00:00:17,567
<i>He'll help you track down Golda.</i>

10
00:00:17,700 --> 00:00:18,667
<i> Theresa...</i>

11
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:20,733
<i>The syndicate following us,
they're here.</i>

12
00:00:20,867 --> 00:00:21,733
<i> It's getting dangerous.</i>

13
00:00:21,867 --> 00:00:23,767
<i>Catalina, you're
stepping in now.</i>

14
00:00:23,900 --> 00:00:26,267
<i>This negotiation
must never leak,</i>

15
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:28,567
<i>because other groups
are already on edge.</i>

16
00:00:28,700 --> 00:00:29,767
<i> If this gets out,</i>

17
00:00:29,900 --> 00:00:31,733
<i>you know exactly
who I'll come after...</i>

18
00:00:31,867 --> 00:00:33,133
<i> you and your Godfather.</i>

19
00:00:33,267 --> 00:00:34,933
<i>You know, even if
I'm the only hope</i>

20
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:37,200
<i>for Miguel to get free,
I don't care anymore.</i>

21
00:00:37,333 --> 00:00:38,700
<i> Suffer, all of you!</i>

22
00:00:38,833 --> 00:00:40,367
<i> I don't care!</i>

23
00:00:40,500 --> 00:00:41,767
<i> Who is that?</i>

24
00:00:41,900 --> 00:00:43,533
<i> She's my husband's mistress.</i>

25
00:00:43,667 --> 00:00:45,800
<i> I thought I could forget.</i>

26
00:00:45,933 --> 00:00:47,300
<i> But seeing that woman...</i>

27
00:00:47,433 --> 00:00:49,067
<i> everything just came back.</i>

28
00:00:49,200 --> 00:00:50,700
<i> Give me one more chance.</i>

29
00:00:50,833 --> 00:00:52,000
<i> I'll search for your family</i>

30
00:00:52,133 --> 00:00:53,767
<i> once I meet with Trigger</i>

31
00:00:53,900 --> 00:00:55,933
<i>and find out
what I need to know.</i>

32
00:00:58,733 --> 00:01:00,500
<i> The one and only...</i>

33
00:01:00,633 --> 00:01:03,400
<i> Catalina Esperanza!</i>

34
00:01:03,533 --> 00:01:06,400
<i> [JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING]</i>

35
00:01:08,900 --> 00:01:18,867
<i> [OBB]</i>

36
00:01:25,367 --> 00:01:26,867
Shoot.

37
00:01:27,000 --> 00:01:28,633
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

38
00:01:28,767 --> 00:01:30,067
Go ahead.

39
00:01:30,200 --> 00:01:32,233
Buddy! Buddy!

40
00:01:32,367 --> 00:01:33,267
Don't aim at him.

41
00:01:33,400 --> 00:01:35,733
That's Andrew Dizon,
a famous vlogger.

42
00:01:35,867 --> 00:01:38,167
Oh, Sir, I'm sorry about that.

43
00:01:38,300 --> 00:01:40,167
Is that so?
All right, all right.

44
00:01:41,200 --> 00:01:43,300
It's okay, it's okay,
I understand.

45
00:01:43,433 --> 00:01:44,533
I'm sorry, Sir.

46
00:01:44,667 --> 00:01:46,567
He's just doing his job.

47
00:01:46,700 --> 00:01:48,267
Apologies, apologies.

48
00:01:48,400 --> 00:01:49,767
Thank you.

49
00:01:50,400 --> 00:01:51,267
Thank you, Sir.
Come on in.

50
00:01:51,400 --> 00:01:53,000
Thank you.

51
00:01:56,300 --> 00:02:00,333
[CROWD APPLAUDING]
[JAZZ MUSIC PLAYING]

52
00:02:17,100 --> 00:02:21,133
[JAZZ MUSIC CONTINUES]

53
00:02:31,833 --> 00:02:32,800
Andrew?

54
00:02:32,933 --> 00:02:34,767
Sister, what are you doing here?

55
00:02:35,533 --> 00:02:37,400
I'm here for Hope Circle,

56
00:02:37,533 --> 00:02:39,633
and I have a meeting
with our potential sponsor.

57
00:02:39,767 --> 00:02:42,000
And you? What are you
doing here?

58
00:02:42,367 --> 00:02:44,400
I'm one of the guests.

59
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:46,600
[SCOFFS]
With that get up?

60
00:02:46,733 --> 00:02:47,800
Long story, Sister.

61
00:02:47,967 --> 00:02:49,067
Anyway, I have to go.

62
00:02:49,200 --> 00:02:50,267
I'm in a hurry.

63
00:02:50,400 --> 00:02:51,767
Okay?

64
00:02:52,300 --> 00:02:53,833
Okay.

65
00:02:53,967 --> 00:02:57,933
[JAZZ MUSIC CONTINUES]

66
00:03:13,800 --> 00:03:17,367
[JAZZ MUSIC CONTINUES]

67
00:03:17,500 --> 00:03:20,733
[PHONE RINGING]

68
00:03:23,900 --> 00:03:25,400
Braggy?

69
00:03:26,000 --> 00:03:28,567
Oh, you're here already?

70
00:03:28,700 --> 00:03:30,833
That's wonderful!

71
00:03:30,967 --> 00:03:33,267
Okay, I'll let Godfather know.

72
00:03:33,400 --> 00:03:37,567
[JAZZ MUSIC CONTINUES]

73
00:03:37,700 --> 00:03:39,700
Joey, go!

74
00:03:39,833 --> 00:03:43,933
[JAZZ MUSIC CONTINUES]

75
00:03:48,767 --> 00:03:52,400
[CROWD CHEERING AND APPLAUDING]

76
00:03:56,567 --> 00:03:58,133
Braggy is here.

77
00:03:58,267 --> 00:04:02,367
[JAZZ MUSIC CONTINUES]

78
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:15,333
[CROWD CHEERING AND APPLAUDING]

79
00:04:15,467 --> 00:04:17,100
Thank you, Catalina.

80
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:20,333
What a stunning performance
to kick off tonight's party.

81
00:04:20,467 --> 00:04:22,733
Now, guests, the dance floor
is now open.

82
00:04:22,867 --> 00:04:24,967
Amazing, amazing!
Let's put it off.

83
00:04:25,367 --> 00:04:26,233
Excuse, excuse.

84
00:04:26,367 --> 00:04:28,033
[CAMERA SHUTTER SNAPPING]

85
00:04:28,200 --> 00:04:32,200
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

86
00:04:44,400 --> 00:04:46,133
How am I doing so far?

87
00:04:46,267 --> 00:04:49,100
Am I a 9 or a perfect 10?

88
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:54,633
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

89
00:05:02,067 --> 00:05:06,867
Oh, maybe you're at 8.5?

90
00:05:07,000 --> 00:05:08,233
Okay.

91
00:05:08,367 --> 00:05:09,500
That's progress.

92
00:05:09,633 --> 00:05:10,800
I'll take it.

93
00:05:10,933 --> 00:05:14,400
Yeah, slowly but surely.

94
00:05:14,533 --> 00:05:18,667
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

95
00:05:22,367 --> 00:05:26,467
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

96
00:05:27,967 --> 00:05:29,567
Are you okay?

97
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:32,300
Yes.

98
00:05:32,433 --> 00:05:35,633
Is it okay if you get me
another drink?

99
00:05:36,367 --> 00:05:39,667
It might just push you
to a solid 10.

100
00:05:39,800 --> 00:05:41,433
Hard.

101
00:05:42,133 --> 00:05:43,833
Whatever it takes.

102
00:05:43,967 --> 00:05:47,933
[INQUISITIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

103
00:05:55,500 --> 00:05:57,733
[LINE RINGS]

104
00:05:57,867 --> 00:05:59,267
Lisa.

105
00:05:59,400 --> 00:06:00,600
It's on.

106
00:06:00,733 --> 00:06:01,733
Copy.

107
00:06:01,867 --> 00:06:04,700
Wait, I've got a bonus.

108
00:06:04,833 --> 00:06:06,300
Bonus?

109
00:06:06,967 --> 00:06:11,067
I know where that ever-sucking
leech, Golda, is hiding.

110
00:06:11,533 --> 00:06:15,833
<i>She's here right under my nose.</i>

111
00:06:16,300 --> 00:06:17,300
All right.

112
00:06:17,433 --> 00:06:18,867
I got this.

113
00:06:21,900 --> 00:06:26,100
What exactly does
our client need, Mr. Braganza?

114
00:06:26,233 --> 00:06:28,667
Glock? Sig sauer? Bareta?

115
00:06:28,800 --> 00:06:31,133
9 millimeter? 45?

116
00:06:31,267 --> 00:06:35,600
Long barrel?
M14? M16? AK-47?

117
00:06:35,733 --> 00:06:36,900
Bazooka? Cannon?

118
00:06:37,033 --> 00:06:39,667
What does your client need?

119
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:42,267
I know Golda told you

120
00:06:42,433 --> 00:06:44,700
who my clients are,

121
00:06:44,833 --> 00:06:46,900
so you also know

122
00:06:47,033 --> 00:06:49,867
I'm not looking for weak guns.

123
00:06:50,000 --> 00:06:52,667
Whatever strong calibers
you mentioned,

124
00:06:53,400 --> 00:06:54,933
I'll take.

125
00:06:55,767 --> 00:06:57,467
No problem.

126
00:06:58,233 --> 00:07:01,567
But it can't go through
the pier.

127
00:07:02,400 --> 00:07:04,267
It has to go through
the backdoor.

128
00:07:04,800 --> 00:07:07,333
Shipment fees will be higher.

129
00:07:07,467 --> 00:07:10,000
Oh, Braggy...

130
00:07:10,133 --> 00:07:12,200
Godfather wants cash upfront,
okay?

131
00:07:12,333 --> 00:07:14,167
Across the board.

132
00:07:15,700 --> 00:07:17,533
No problem...

133
00:07:18,033 --> 00:07:22,300
as long as the transaction is
clean and there are no leaks.

134
00:07:22,433 --> 00:07:24,367
Because if anything leaks,

135
00:07:24,500 --> 00:07:26,367
the deal stops...

136
00:07:27,067 --> 00:07:31,400
and so does anyone who talks.

137
00:07:31,533 --> 00:07:35,800
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

138
00:07:46,567 --> 00:07:50,367
Do you know what this is,
Mr. Braganza?

139
00:07:52,967 --> 00:07:57,800
A burnay jar, made in Ilocos.

140
00:07:58,533 --> 00:08:02,033
It's been in my family for over
a hundred years.

141
00:08:03,733 --> 00:08:05,600
Strong,

142
00:08:06,033 --> 00:08:08,100
well-crafted,

143
00:08:09,200 --> 00:08:11,233
no cracks,

144
00:08:11,833 --> 00:08:14,067
no leaks.

145
00:08:16,300 --> 00:08:19,633
That's how my bloodline is,
Mr. Braganza.

146
00:08:21,400 --> 00:08:23,500
That's my reputation.

147
00:08:23,633 --> 00:08:26,033
I don't care...

148
00:08:26,167 --> 00:08:29,533
how big your client is.

149
00:08:30,433 --> 00:08:33,000
I don't need you.

150
00:08:33,133 --> 00:08:35,867
And I especially
don't need your threats

151
00:08:36,000 --> 00:08:38,900
in my own home.

152
00:08:41,767 --> 00:08:43,967
I might not hold back.

153
00:08:45,833 --> 00:08:49,600
I could smash this burnay
on your head.

154
00:08:49,733 --> 00:08:53,800
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

155
00:09:06,467 --> 00:09:08,667
Relax, Godfather.

156
00:09:08,800 --> 00:09:12,833
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

157
00:09:20,833 --> 00:09:23,233
Where are you, Golda?

158
00:09:23,367 --> 00:09:25,067
Ah, Joey.

159
00:09:25,200 --> 00:09:26,900
Oh, have you seen her?

160
00:09:27,033 --> 00:09:27,900
No.

161
00:09:28,067 --> 00:09:30,000
- Still not here?
- Still not here.

162
00:09:33,533 --> 00:09:35,267
Andrew, what are you doing here?

163
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:37,433
Oh, what are you wearing?

164
00:09:38,133 --> 00:09:39,867
Put this on.

165
00:09:43,033 --> 00:09:46,633
Wait, didn't I tell you
to get out?

166
00:09:46,767 --> 00:09:50,167
Joey, the syndicate looking
for you, they're here.

167
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:51,833
We searched for Golda,
but she got away.

168
00:09:51,967 --> 00:09:53,000
She's gone.

169
00:09:53,133 --> 00:09:55,100
We'll deal with Golda later.
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

170
00:09:55,233 --> 00:09:56,967
Okay? Let's go.

171
00:10:01,767 --> 00:10:03,200
Mom?

172
00:10:03,333 --> 00:10:05,800
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

173
00:10:07,900 --> 00:10:09,500
Well...

174
00:10:09,633 --> 00:10:11,500
The quality is solid.
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

175
00:10:12,200 --> 00:10:14,767
Everyone I know
in the Philippines

176
00:10:14,900 --> 00:10:15,967
with a private army

177
00:10:16,100 --> 00:10:18,100
get their supply from him.

178
00:10:19,867 --> 00:10:21,667
So, 2 weeks?

179
00:10:23,567 --> 00:10:25,267
Deal.

180
00:10:25,400 --> 00:10:29,500
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

181
00:10:38,767 --> 00:10:40,367
It's a deal.

182
00:10:40,833 --> 00:10:42,200
Wow!

183
00:10:42,333 --> 00:10:44,200
Congrats, boys!

184
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,767
Congratulations to us.
[CURIOUS MUSIC PLAYING]

185
00:10:47,900 --> 00:10:49,633
Congratulations, Godfather.

186
00:10:49,767 --> 00:10:52,733
The shipment from Valdoria
arrives tomorrow.

187
00:10:52,867 --> 00:10:55,300
I will have your arms ready
by then.

188
00:10:57,033 --> 00:10:59,833
[PHONE RINGING]

189
00:11:04,800 --> 00:11:06,067
Hello?

190
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:07,633
Braggy!

191
00:11:07,800 --> 00:11:09,800
Do you still remember me?
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

192
00:11:10,433 --> 00:11:12,000
Who is this?

193
00:11:12,700 --> 00:11:14,933
Let's just say I know
what you're cooking up

194
00:11:15,067 --> 00:11:17,067
with Godfather.

195
00:11:17,200 --> 00:11:18,433
How are you?

196
00:11:18,567 --> 00:11:19,900
So, the deal's done?

197
00:11:20,033 --> 00:11:21,467
Don't worry.

198
00:11:21,600 --> 00:11:24,300
We'll be watching
that deal closely.

199
00:11:24,433 --> 00:11:27,033
If this transaction
gets messed up,

200
00:11:27,833 --> 00:11:30,900
I'll make sure you'll grow
too lazy to even breathe...

201
00:11:31,033 --> 00:11:32,933
and the same goes
for your family.

202
00:11:36,567 --> 00:11:38,800
How did someone find out
about this transaction?

203
00:11:38,933 --> 00:11:40,233
You liars!
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:11:40,367 --> 00:11:42,900
Oh, Braggy...

205
00:11:43,067 --> 00:11:44,733
Braggy, believe me.
No one...

206
00:11:44,867 --> 00:11:46,867
no one leaked the information!

207
00:11:47,900 --> 00:11:52,067
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

208
00:11:55,033 --> 00:11:56,867
What is she doing here?

209
00:11:58,767 --> 00:12:00,533
Come on, let's go to her.

210
00:12:02,533 --> 00:12:04,933
Don't be stupid, Braganza.

211
00:12:05,067 --> 00:12:07,133
You're inside my house.

212
00:12:07,267 --> 00:12:09,767
You won't leave
this place alive.

213
00:12:09,900 --> 00:12:11,200
There's only one way
to settle this.

214
00:12:11,333 --> 00:12:13,833
Let's pull these triggers

215
00:12:13,967 --> 00:12:17,200
and find out
who the real fool is.

216
00:12:17,667 --> 00:12:21,767
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

217
00:12:34,500 --> 00:12:38,267
- [GUN FIRING]
- [GOLDA SHRIEKING]

218
00:12:38,400 --> 00:12:41,533
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

219
00:12:41,667 --> 00:12:45,800
[CROWD CLAMORING]

220
00:12:49,333 --> 00:12:51,533
Get down! Get down!

221
00:12:51,667 --> 00:12:55,100
- [GUN FIRING]
- [CROWD CLAMORING]

222
00:12:56,367 --> 00:12:57,500
It's a shootout!

223
00:12:57,633 --> 00:12:58,833
My gosh.

224
00:12:58,967 --> 00:13:00,833
Where did that come from?

225
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:06,267
- [GUN FIRING]
- [CROWD CLAMORING]

226
00:13:08,100 --> 00:13:09,633
Mom!

227
00:13:17,200 --> 00:13:19,067
What was that?
Let's go!

228
00:13:19,200 --> 00:13:23,300
- [GUN FIRING]
- [GOLDA WHIMPERING]

229
00:13:23,467 --> 00:13:27,633
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

230
00:13:29,933 --> 00:13:32,033
[GOLDA WHIMPERING]

231
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:36,467
[GUN FIRING]

232
00:13:39,100 --> 00:13:41,800
[GOLDA WHIMPERING]

233
00:13:46,433 --> 00:13:47,567
Mom!

234
00:13:47,700 --> 00:13:48,800
I need to go to her.

235
00:13:48,933 --> 00:13:50,400
I'll be the one to go inside.

236
00:13:50,533 --> 00:13:52,200
I'm coming with you.

237
00:13:52,333 --> 00:13:54,300
Joey, no,
it's dangerous, please.

238
00:13:54,433 --> 00:13:55,233
I'll handle it.

239
00:13:55,400 --> 00:13:57,133
My sister's in there anyway.

240
00:13:57,267 --> 00:13:59,367
Okay? I'll take care of them.

241
00:13:59,500 --> 00:14:00,733
Okay?

242
00:14:00,867 --> 00:14:02,500
Go to Jin Ho.

243
00:14:02,633 --> 00:14:04,300
He's outside.

244
00:14:05,867 --> 00:14:08,867
Andrew, don't leave mom, okay?

245
00:14:09,500 --> 00:14:10,267
I won't.

246
00:14:10,400 --> 00:14:12,567
- Call me.
- Let's go.

247
00:14:12,700 --> 00:14:19,467
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

248
00:14:19,600 --> 00:14:20,300
You're an animal, Godfather!
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING♪]

249
00:14:21,167 --> 00:14:23,267
I knew it,
you can't be trusted!

250
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,867
You're going
straight to hell now!

251
00:14:25,500 --> 00:14:26,600
You should go first!

252
00:14:26,733 --> 00:14:28,733
Godfather!
[GUN FIRING]

253
00:14:28,900 --> 00:14:30,367
[WHIMPERS]

254
00:14:30,633 --> 00:14:33,767
[GUN FIRING]

255
00:14:35,267 --> 00:14:38,000
[GUN FIRING]

256
00:14:42,833 --> 00:14:44,433
[GUN FIRES]

257
00:14:45,133 --> 00:14:47,233
Ma'am Yvette! Ma'am Yvette!

258
00:14:47,367 --> 00:14:48,700
Ma'am Yvette!

259
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,167
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

260
00:14:51,300 --> 00:14:53,667
[WOMEN WHIMPERING]

261
00:14:53,800 --> 00:14:55,467
Miss Clarissa...

262
00:14:57,067 --> 00:15:00,033
[GUN FIRING]

263
00:15:02,233 --> 00:15:03,733
We're wiped out!

264
00:15:05,033 --> 00:15:08,767
[GUN FIRING]

265
00:15:08,900 --> 00:15:10,733
Boss Braganza, we're here!

266
00:15:10,867 --> 00:15:13,200
- Are you okay?
- Cover me!

267
00:15:13,333 --> 00:15:17,267
[GUN FIRING]

268
00:15:19,733 --> 00:15:21,367
Go after them!

269
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:24,933
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

270
00:15:25,067 --> 00:15:27,767
[GUN FIRING]

271
00:15:30,867 --> 00:15:33,333
You're an idiot, Matias.

272
00:15:33,800 --> 00:15:35,000
Exciting, right?

273
00:15:35,167 --> 00:15:37,333
Exciting your face.

274
00:15:37,467 --> 00:15:39,200
You should've at least
told me earlier

275
00:15:39,333 --> 00:15:41,667
so I could've gotten out sooner.

276
00:15:41,800 --> 00:15:43,167
What if I got hit?
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

277
00:15:43,300 --> 00:15:44,967
But you didn't, right?

278
00:15:45,100 --> 00:15:46,633
So just relax.

279
00:15:46,767 --> 00:15:48,467
<i>It's best that you
should go home already.</i>

280
00:15:48,600 --> 00:15:50,367
<i> Let's celebrate.</i>

281
00:15:50,500 --> 00:15:52,133
Our job is done.

282
00:15:52,267 --> 00:15:53,867
What about Golda?

283
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:55,500
Don't worry about that.

284
00:15:55,633 --> 00:15:57,933
Leave her to Braganza and
Godfather.

285
00:15:58,067 --> 00:15:59,367
<i> They'll surely pin</i>

286
00:15:59,500 --> 00:16:00,800
<i> the leaked transaction on her.</i>

287
00:16:00,933 --> 00:16:04,000
Golda definitely won't make it
out alive.

288
00:16:04,567 --> 00:16:06,033
Godfather...
Godfather...

289
00:16:06,167 --> 00:16:07,833
Godfather, thank you, thank you.

290
00:16:08,000 --> 00:16:09,333
Golda...

291
00:16:09,467 --> 00:16:12,500
You're putting me in
a difficult position here.

292
00:16:12,633 --> 00:16:13,667
Tell me the truth.

293
00:16:13,800 --> 00:16:16,733
Who did you tell
about this transaction?

294
00:16:16,867 --> 00:16:17,867
Godfather, no one!

295
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,533
Stop pretending!

296
00:16:19,667 --> 00:16:20,600
Godfather...

297
00:16:20,733 --> 00:16:22,433
You're the only one
who could've leaked this.

298
00:16:22,567 --> 00:16:24,567
So, tell me...

299
00:16:24,700 --> 00:16:26,267
Who do you work for, huh?

300
00:16:26,400 --> 00:16:29,400
Otherwise, you're not leaving
here alive.

301
00:16:29,533 --> 00:16:31,000
Godfather, Godfather...

302
00:16:31,133 --> 00:16:32,667
Godfather, I could never
do that to you.

303
00:16:32,800 --> 00:16:34,400
Godfather, please believe me.

304
00:16:34,533 --> 00:16:37,133
I could never betray you,
Godfather.

305
00:16:37,400 --> 00:16:42,533
[GUN FIRING]
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

306
00:16:46,267 --> 00:16:49,433
[GUN FIRING]

307
00:16:56,133 --> 00:16:58,067
[GRUNTS]
Wait! Wait! It's me!

308
00:16:58,200 --> 00:16:59,900
Will you just shut up?

309
00:17:00,033 --> 00:17:02,033
Let's get out of here
before we get dragged into this.

310
00:17:02,167 --> 00:17:03,700
Boss Idol!

311
00:17:05,733 --> 00:17:08,633
- [GUN FIRING]
- [CLARISSA SHRIEKING]

312
00:17:08,767 --> 00:17:11,767
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

313
00:17:11,900 --> 00:17:15,667
[GUN FIRING]

314
00:17:18,367 --> 00:17:19,800
[CLARISSA SHRIEKS]

315
00:17:21,267 --> 00:17:22,600
Boss Idol...

316
00:17:23,100 --> 00:17:24,200
Are you okay?

317
00:17:24,333 --> 00:17:25,933
I thought I was going to die.

318
00:17:26,067 --> 00:17:27,533
- Thank you.
- Don't worry about it.

319
00:17:27,667 --> 00:17:29,633
But we have to leave right now.

320
00:17:29,767 --> 00:17:31,867
We can't, Ma'am Yvette...

321
00:17:32,000 --> 00:17:33,867
Ma'am Yvette isn't here yet.

322
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,667
Where is she?

323
00:17:35,800 --> 00:17:39,433
[GUN FIRING]

324
00:17:41,333 --> 00:17:44,767
[GUN FIRING]

325
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:47,933
Please let me go, Godfather.

326
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:51,167
After I hit Braganza
with bullets,

327
00:17:51,300 --> 00:17:53,467
you're next.

328
00:17:54,067 --> 00:17:55,767
Godfather, Godfather...

329
00:17:55,900 --> 00:17:58,300
[GUN FIRING]

330
00:17:58,433 --> 00:17:59,967
[SHRIEKS]

331
00:18:02,133 --> 00:18:03,767
Golda!

332
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:05,833
Jin Ho, Jin Ho,
let's go, let's go.

333
00:18:05,967 --> 00:18:06,967
We have to meet Andrew
in the airbnb.

334
00:18:07,100 --> 00:18:08,567
- Let's go!
- Let's go.

335
00:18:11,933 --> 00:18:13,367
Theresa...

336
00:18:13,500 --> 00:18:14,667
Weren't we leaving?

337
00:18:14,800 --> 00:18:16,967
Are we going to go or not?

338
00:18:17,100 --> 00:18:21,700
[INTENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

339
00:18:22,200 --> 00:18:23,400
- Jin Ho, let's go!
- Jin Ho!

340
00:18:24,967 --> 00:18:27,200
You guys go ahead.
[BRAZEN MUSIC PLAYING]

341
00:18:27,333 --> 00:18:29,933
I can't let Theresa
get away again.

342
00:18:30,067 --> 00:18:31,400
Where are you going?
What's your plan?

343
00:18:31,533 --> 00:18:33,333
I'm going to catch her.

344
00:18:33,467 --> 00:18:34,900
What about us?

345
00:18:36,867 --> 00:18:38,967
Go to my car and drive.

346
00:18:39,100 --> 00:18:40,200
Get out of here.

347
00:18:40,333 --> 00:18:41,033
What about you?

348
00:18:41,167 --> 00:18:42,633
Don't worry about me.

349
00:18:45,700 --> 00:18:48,000
Come on.
Let's go, let's go!

350
00:18:49,233 --> 00:18:53,033
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

351
00:18:53,167 --> 00:18:54,833
[CAR ENGINE STARTS]

352
00:18:56,167 --> 00:18:57,867
Let's get out of here!

353
00:18:58,000 --> 00:19:00,633
[REVVING]

354
00:19:00,767 --> 00:19:04,933
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

355
00:19:14,933 --> 00:19:18,833
[BRAZEN MUSIC CONTINUES]

356
00:19:21,467 --> 00:19:23,467
[ENGINE STARTS]

357
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:30,067
Oh, seatbelt, seatbelt.

358
00:19:31,033 --> 00:19:33,433
Wait, wait, hold on.
Let's not leave yet.

359
00:19:33,567 --> 00:19:36,100
- Why?
- My mom is still in there!

360
00:19:36,233 --> 00:19:38,233
I want to make sure she's okay.

361
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:41,100
Where's Andrew?
Why is he taking so long?

362
00:19:41,233 --> 00:19:43,200
Andrew? Can't you hear
the gunshots?

363
00:19:43,333 --> 00:19:45,833
Boss Budol wouldn't rush in
there for no reason.

364
00:19:45,967 --> 00:19:47,300
And we're not allowed
to stay here,

365
00:19:47,433 --> 00:19:48,667
so we have to go!
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

366
00:19:48,800 --> 00:19:50,200
- But...
- But what?

367
00:19:50,333 --> 00:19:52,800
What if your mom gets out
and sees you here?

368
00:19:52,933 --> 00:19:54,567
Huh? What then? Will you be able
to explain that to her?

369
00:19:54,700 --> 00:19:56,467
Do you even have an excuse
ready?

370
00:19:59,000 --> 00:20:00,500
- Oh, all right, all right.
- Let's go.

371
00:20:00,633 --> 00:20:03,300
Andrew probably won't abandon
my mom, right?

372
00:20:05,467 --> 00:20:08,233
[REVVING]

373
00:20:08,367 --> 00:20:12,133
[GUN FIRING]
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

374
00:20:14,433 --> 00:20:15,733
Just follow behind me.

375
00:20:15,867 --> 00:20:17,133
Hurry.

376
00:20:17,267 --> 00:20:21,367
[GUN FIRING]

377
00:20:21,500 --> 00:20:24,800
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

378
00:20:27,867 --> 00:20:29,233
Ma'am Yvette...

379
00:20:29,367 --> 00:20:32,900
[GUN FIRING]

380
00:20:33,033 --> 00:20:37,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

381
00:20:37,700 --> 00:20:41,933
[GUN FIRING]

382
00:20:44,867 --> 00:20:47,100
[GUN FIRING]

383
00:20:48,033 --> 00:20:50,100
You have nowhere left to run,
Braganza!

384
00:20:50,233 --> 00:20:52,033
This is where it ends for you!

385
00:20:52,167 --> 00:20:54,400
-[GUN FIRES]
- We can't get trapped here!

386
00:20:56,100 --> 00:20:58,100
[GUN FIRES]

387
00:21:00,967 --> 00:21:03,400
- [LAMP SHATTERS]
- [GUN FIRING]

388
00:21:03,933 --> 00:21:05,333
[GASPS]

389
00:21:08,500 --> 00:21:10,200
- [GUN FIRES]
- [SHRIEKS]

390
00:21:10,333 --> 00:21:12,100
Let's go, come on!

391
00:21:13,633 --> 00:21:15,200
Miss Clarissa, this way!

392
00:21:15,333 --> 00:21:17,700
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

393
00:21:17,833 --> 00:21:20,900
[GUN FIRING]

394
00:21:22,633 --> 00:21:25,200
Go after that animal!

395
00:21:25,667 --> 00:21:28,333
Don't let him get out alive!

396
00:21:29,033 --> 00:21:31,067
Find Golda!

397
00:21:31,200 --> 00:21:35,267
[INTENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

398
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:41,167
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

399
00:21:43,000 --> 00:21:44,600
I need to get out of here.

400
00:21:44,733 --> 00:21:45,667
Where's Theresa?

401
00:21:45,800 --> 00:21:47,333
We didn't gain anything
from this mission.

402
00:21:47,467 --> 00:21:49,433
No, we still found something.

403
00:21:49,567 --> 00:21:50,167
Golda?

404
00:21:50,300 --> 00:21:52,100
Let me out of here!

405
00:21:52,233 --> 00:21:53,300
What the heck!

406
00:21:53,433 --> 00:21:54,333
Tell me everything you know

407
00:21:54,467 --> 00:21:56,167
about how my father was set up.

408
00:21:56,300 --> 00:21:59,367
Miguel, Trigger wants to talk
to you tomorrow.

409
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:01,767
And then what, you're all going
to gang up on me again?

410
00:22:01,900 --> 00:22:03,967
It's up to you
if you show up or not.

411
00:22:04,100 --> 00:22:06,133
I know I'm Berdugo's
next target.

412
00:22:06,267 --> 00:22:07,000
Berdugo?

413
00:22:07,133 --> 00:22:08,800
He's the leader
of the syndicates.

414
00:22:08,933 --> 00:22:11,500
I need to find out
where I can find Berdugo.

415
00:22:11,633 --> 00:22:13,533
Wait, you don't know
Vicente Alcala?

416
00:22:13,667 --> 00:22:15,800
Someone saved me. Boss Idol did.

417
00:22:15,967 --> 00:22:17,633
What?
How?

418
00:22:17,767 --> 00:22:19,400
He's actually kind, isn't he?

419
00:22:19,533 --> 00:22:20,833
- [KNOCK ON THE DOOR]
- Golda?

420
00:22:20,967 --> 00:22:22,400
What are you doing there?

421
00:22:22,533 --> 00:22:24,033
The person I'm watching hasn't
come out yet.

422
00:22:24,167 --> 00:22:25,067
I think she escaped.

423
00:22:25,200 --> 00:22:26,167
What? How?

424
00:22:26,300 --> 00:22:27,700
Maybe she went through the
window.

425
00:22:27,833 --> 00:22:28,900
Then let's go. Let's find her.

426
00:22:29,033 --> 00:22:30,600
We could have avoided this

427
00:22:30,733 --> 00:22:33,400
if you had made sure
she was dead.

428
00:22:33,533 --> 00:22:35,767
Now find that woman.
Now!
